  "summary": "The SF Standard reports that California police agencies are routinely violating SB 34 by sharing ALPR data with federal agencies, including searches labeled 'ICE case,' 'DEA Assist,' and 'FBI.' The state AG has issued warning letters to at least 20 agencies since June 2024, but agencies including Riverside and Sacramento County sheriffs appeared to continue violations after warnings. Advocates and SB 34's author call for aggressive enforcement, while Flock has rolled out new features to block ICE/immigration-related searches.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "An April search by the California Highway Patrol of 845 ALPR systems, including Oakland's, was labeled \"ICE case,\" raising concerns that local police may have aided federal immigration enforcement.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "logs obtained by The Standard show that, less than two months later, the department was still searching ALPR data for investigations related to the FBI and U.S. Postal Inspection Service.",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    },
    {
      "quote": "I don't think the necessary intent of that law was to exclude out-of-state agencies",
      "paragraph_idx": 29
    },
    {
      "quote": "It's the fruit of the poisonous tree",
      "paragraph_idx": 31
    },
    {
      "quote": "On Tuesday, Flock unveiled a separate feature in California that it says will automatically flag and block searches that include keywords like \"immigration\" and \"ICE.\"",
      "paragraph_idx": 40
    }
  ],
